{"id": "EUVD-2026-103058", "enisaUuid": "2d736396-3953-30de-9218-7c9d8f193aef", "description": "OpenBMB StaffDeck through 0.5.6 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to forge administrator session tokens using the hard-coded default app_secret. Attackers can sign an HMAC-SHA256 token for the seeded 'admin' user in 'tenant_demo' to gain full tenant administration, including stored model and channel credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:19:00", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/staffdeck-default-token-signing-secret-auth-bypass", "https://github.com/OpenBMB/StaffDeck/blob/v0.5.6/backend/app/config.py#L10", "https://github.com/OpenBMB/StaffDeck/blob/v0.5.6/backend/app/security/auth.py#L96-L98", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openbmb-staffdeck-through-0.5.6-authentication-bypass-via-hard-coded-session-secret"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111636", "GHSA-m82j-2j7c-gx6q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dc3dd813-f539-34c9-9711-5fcac10f83ce", "product": {"name": "StaffDeck", "vendor": {"name": "OpenBMB"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7f1cb53d-f7bc-307c-871d-a45786dd43bf", "vendor": {"name": "OpenBMB"}}], "isExploited": false}